<title>GERMANY: German intvn board details free market grain bids.</title>
<headline>German intvn board details free market grain bids.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders bid for the export of 12,000 tonnes of free market barley with an 11.96 Ecus a tonne rebate, grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders also bid for the export of 1,100 tonnes of free market rye at a subsidy level of 22.98 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>The EU cereals management committee will decide on the bids at its weekly meeting later today.</p>
